{"name":"City Street","hex":"#bab2ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"city","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large settlement, bigger than a town; sometimes with a specific legal definition, depending on the place.","A settlement granted special status by royal charter or letters patent; traditionally, a settlement with a cathedral regardless of size."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/city"},{"term":"street","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A paved part of road, usually in a village or a town.","A road as above, but including the sidewalks (pavements) and buildings."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build or equip with streets.","To eject; to throw onto the streets."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/street"}],"entries":[{"title":"City","blocks":[{"text":"A city is a human settlement of a substantial size. The term \"city\" has different meanings around the world and in some places the settlement can be very small. Even where the term is limited to larger settlements, there is no universally agreed definition of the lower numerical boundary for their size. In a more specific sense, a city can be defined as a permanent and densely populated place with administratively defined boundaries whose members work primarily on non-agricultural tasks. Cities generally have extensive systems for housing, transportation, sanitation, utilities, land use, production of goods, and communication. Their density facilitates interaction between people, government organizations, and businesses, sometimes benefiting different parties in the process, such as improving the efficiency of goods and service distribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg/330px-Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City","wikidata":"Q515"},{"title":"Street","blocks":[{"text":"A street is a public thoroughfare in a city, town or village, typically lined with buildings on one or both sides. Streets often include pavements (sidewalks), pedestrian crossings, and sometimes amenities like streetlights or benches. A street can be as simple as a level patch of dirt, but is more often paved with a hard, durable surface such as tarmac, concrete, cobblestone or brick. It can be designed for both social activity and movement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Typical_Street_In_The_Royal_Borough_Of_Kensington_And_Chelsea_In_London.jpg/330px-Typical_Street_In_The_Royal_Borough_Of_Kensington_And_Chelsea_In_London.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Street","wikidata":"Q79007"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Lagos-centre-from-executive-lounge-Continental-hotel-2026-IMG_7970_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Lagos-centre-from-executive-lounge-Continental-hotel-2026-IMG_7970_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Lagos-centre-from-executive-lounge-Continental-hotel-2026-IMG_7970_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Lagos-centre-from-executive-lounge-Continental-hotel-2026-IMG_7970_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Lagos-centre-from-executive-lounge-Continental-hotel-2026-IMG_7970_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Lagos-centre-from-executive-lounge-Continental-hotel-2026-IMG_7970_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALagos-centre-from-executive-lounge-Continental-hotel-2026-IMG_7970_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t